# The exact `wolf --version` string that commit produces (first line; the
# binary also prints a second line naming its lupin pairing — 0.1.24 at this
# pin, up from 0.1.23 at v0.2.3). `lspconf doctor` fails on a mismatch: a stale
# local `wolf` producing green transcripts is the failure mode the pin exists
# to prevent.
#
# D57 decides the shape. A build is a release build only when the builder
# stamps BOTH `WOLF_COMMIT=<short sha>` and `WOLF_RELEASE=v{crate version}`,
# and the second is granted only when that exact tag points at HEAD. This pin
# is at v0.2.4, so a release build prints the BARE version and the pin clause.
# An unstamped build still prints `+dev.unknown` — the string any trunk build
# of the same crate version prints, which is exactly the stale-binary hole —
# so the pinned string remains a stamped build's, and `cargo xtask dist` in
# the submodule is the builder that computes the stamp (README §Running the
# server lane locally; its plain-cargo recipe cannot grant the release half).
#
# `xtask compat`'s `version_number` reads the number out of this string; it
# learned semver build metadata at le03 and takes the bare tag form
# unchanged — `0.2.4`, no `+` to strip. Asserted in xtask/src/compat.rs.
#
# SEVEN HEX DIGITS FOR THE THIRD PIN RUNNING, and wolf-lang#199 reproduces on
# this box at THIS commit exactly as le06 measured it at the last one. le05
# derived the mechanism with arithmetic: `git rev-parse --short` sizes its AUTO
# abbreviation to the object count of the clone it runs in, so the width is a
# property of the BUILDER'S CLONE and never of the commit. le06 showed two
# clones on one box disagreeing at one commit. le07 re-runs that measurement
# and gets the same split:
#
#   * the binary installed at ~/.local/bin/wolf prints `pin 982f857` — SEVEN;
#   * `git rev-parse --short 982f8578…` in THIS repo's `upstream/` submodule
#     answers `982f8578` — EIGHT.
#
# Three consecutive pins, three identical splits. Nothing about the commit
# changed between the two readings; the line below records what the ACQUIRED
# artifact prints, because that is what CI acquires and what a user runs. A
# locally built submodule binary on a large clone still fails `doctor` here,
# and that refusal is the pin doing its job.
#
# The defect is upstream, in D57's clause being clone-dependent at all, and it
# stays filed as wolf-lang#199 — see docs/COMPAT.md.
version = "wolf 0.2.4 (wolfgang, pin 982f857)"
